# makepkg's working files. The PKGBUILD and its companions are tracked;
# nothing makepkg produces is.
#
# scripts/linux/build.sh --packages exports SRCDEST/BUILDDIR/PKGDEST so none of
# this lands here in the first place — build/ and dist/ are ignored wholesale at
# the repo root, which is a far stronger guarantee than the patterns below.
# These exist for the case where makepkg is run BY HAND from this directory,
# where its defaults put everything in $startdir, i.e. right here.
#
# A `git+https://` source makes makepkg keep a BARE CLONE OF THE WHOLE
# REPOSITORY at packaging/arch/streamer/ if SRCDEST isn't set — a
# .gitignore entry is a second line of defence; the SRCDEST export is the
# first.
streamer/
src/
pkg/
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.pkg.tar.zst.sig
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
